Errors
------
  |->1. Syntax Error - not following python rules 
	------------
		|->We can't execute single line of code
 

  |->2. Logical Error - following python rules , but logical mistakes/correction - Exception
	---------------
		|->Exit Signal  
                |--> To avoid this Exit state - we can write exception block //Handle Exception
	try
	except
	else
	finally
	-------------//python keywords 


	try:
	   <code - initialization> / monitoring block
	except <ExcepionName> as eobj:
	   Handle the Error
	else:
	   There is no Error
	finally:
	   Always running block



    try:
	var = 10
	print(var)
    except NameError as eobj:
	print(eobj)
    else:
	var = var + 100
        print("var=",var)
    finally:
	print("Thank you")


   try:
     fobj = open('filename','r')
   except FileNotFoundError as eobj:
     print(eobj)
   else:
     s = fobj.read()
     print(s)
   finally:
     fobj.close()


    try:
      L = [10,20,30]
      print(L[9])
    except NameError as eobj:
      print(eobj)
    except KeyError as eobj:
      print(eobj)
    except IndexErro as eobj:
      print(eobj)
    else:
	print(L)
    finally:
        print("Thank you")

